maria: heads-up — the .NET sample in the README has a couple of copy/paste issues causing deadlocks and incorrect retry behavior. spotted during a customer onboarding.

aj: ugh. which file?
\bmaria: quickstart/csharp/README.md — there's code doing `.Result` on async network calls and setting headers in the wrong place. simple to reproduce locally: high qps -> intermittent 429 + stuck threads.
\baj: yeah `.Result` on http calls in ASP/.NET is a classic deadlock footgun. also iirc we didn't handle Retry-After at all in that snippet.
\bmaria: exact bad snippet I pasted into their app:```csharp
var client = new HttpClient();
var token = GetToken();
var response = client.PostAsync(url, content).Result; // blocking call
client.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization = new AuthenticationHeaderValue("Bearer", token); // set after send
if (response.StatusCode == (HttpStatusCode)429) {
    // nothing — sample doesn't show retry handling
}
```
\bben: yikes. two problems: blocking call + header set after send. also no handling for Retry-After header which the infra returns often.
\bmaria: proposed minimal fix (async/await + check Retry-After):```csharp
using var client = new HttpClient();
client.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization = new AuthenticationHeaderValue("Bearer", token);
var response = await client.PostAsync(url, content);
if (response.StatusCode == (HttpStatusCode)429) {
    var retryAfter = response.Headers.RetryAfter?.Delta ?? TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2);
    await Task.Delay(retryAfter);
    response = await client.PostAsync(url, content);
}
```
\blili: can we also show a tiny DelegatingHandler example or mention Polly for production? lowers chance folks copy/paste bad retry loops.
\baj: yeah add a note: "for production use a resilient handler (Polly) or built-in SDK retry" and a small snippet referencing Polly would be fine.
\bmaria: i'll open a PR with the async fix + Retry-After example. can someone add the parity note for python/js and a short test that ensures sample compiles (net6) so it doesn't regress?
\bben: can do parity notes for python/js. i'll add a quick integration check in the docs CI to `dotnet build` the sample folder. (+1 :thumbsup:)
